    live_deploy: belt/publication watched-dir controls require the step (review 95659)
    
    the_belt_path_unit_reads_its_watched_dirs / the_publication_path_unit_reads_its_watched_dirs returned
    Absent => true when srv1_steps() had no such step — a decoration that could go green while checking
    nothing if srv1 stopped owning a .path unit (guarantee_ladder: "a check whose forbidden state is
    expressible nowhere it runs is a decoration").
    
    Fix: srv1 MUST own a BeltEventPathUnit and a PublicationHelperPathUnit step; Absent is now a fixture
    defect and returns false, so the check is only green via the Present arm comparing the roster row to the
    DirectoryNotEmpty dirs of the unit's own rendered file (and non-empty).
    
    Verified: both still PASS on base-matched seed sha256 900599bd... (Rust = branch base da9e9f5, src
    clean), confirming the Present arm is taken — srv1 does own these .path units.
    
    Node: deploy-intent-owns-artifact-closure (node://adhoc-3e6e9bfb-d59).

